{"title":"Career roadmap — Food Technologist","role":"Food Technologist","summary":"A Food Technologist applies food science, chemistry, microbiology, processing technology, nutrition and quality systems to develop, manufacture, test and improve food products. The role spans food processing, product development, quality control, food safety, sensory evaluation, packaging, shelf-life, formulation and regulatory compliance.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Food Science & Nutrition"},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"★★★★★ — B.Sc. Food Science & Nutrition is a strong entry pathway, especially for food processing, QC/QA and product-development roles."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build food chemistry, microbiology, processing, nutrition and laboratory skills"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Food Technologist → QC/QA Executive → Product Development Executive"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior Food Technologist → R&D / QA Manager → Product Development Manager"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead food innovation, manufacturing, food safety, quality and sustainable product development"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Core learning","Practical exposure"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Food chemistry, biology, biochemistry, nutrition, microbiology"},{"text":"Basic food analysis and laboratory work"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Food processing, preservation, food microbiology, packaging"},{"text":"Processing experiments and product formulation"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Food safety, HACCP, quality control, sensory science, shelf-life"},{"text":"Food-industry internship"}],[{"text":"Year 4 / Honours"},{"text":"Product development, regulatory affairs, advanced processing, f